      "summary": "The previous stream-bound findings appear addressed, but comment-aware parsing is still needed to prevent a crafted /Length comment from bypassing the preflight limit.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 562,
          "message": "The stream-length lookup can trust a /Length entry inside a PDF comment, allowing oversized text content to bypass preflight. Skip comments when parsing dictionary tokens.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "TryReadStreamLength uses FindPdfToken to select the first /Length token in a stream dictionary. FindPdfToken does not skip PDF comments, so a commented-out /Length entry can be parsed as the stream length.",
            "failureScenario": "A PDF dictionary contains a comment with `/Length 1` before its real `/Length` entry. The preflight records a one-byte stream and can miss a later text-showing operator, then starts the worker; PdfPig ignores the comment and reads the actual oversized stream. Repeated page references can therefore bypass the text-source bound. OWASP A04:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "security-reviewer",
      "reviewType": "security",
